    "# Katalon Head of Data — Technical Prototype Pack\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook consolidates **5 working prototypes** that demonstrate the data + AI engineering patterns a Head of Data candidate should be able to read, explain, and modify on the whiteboard:\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Prototype | Domain | Stack |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| A | CDC dedup → silver (idempotent merge with `aggregate_version`) | Streaming → Lakehouse | PySpark + Delta Lake |\n",
    "| B | Flakiness SQL runner (synthetic data) | Quality Analytics | PySpark SQL / Spark SQL |\n",
    "| C | Reconciliation job (producer vs accepted vs silver vs served) | Reliability | PySpark + Delta Lake |\n",
    "| D | Retrieval evaluation harness | AI / RAG | Pure Python |\n",
    "| E | Idempotent outbox for agent tool calls | Agents / Reliability | Python + sqlite3 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Target runtime:** Databricks Runtime 14.x LTS+ (Python 3.10, PySpark 3.5, Delta Lake 3.x).\n",
    "\n",
    "Run all cells top-to-bottom. Every prototype ends with a `[PASS]` assertion so the demo visibly passes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Prototype A — CDC dedup → silver (idempotent merge with `aggregate_version`)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this proves:** Late, out-of-order CDC events from a test-execution stream can be merged into a `silver` Delta table without producing duplicate `final_result` rows, even when duplicates, retries, and reordering arrive together.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the panel tests:** Your understanding of idempotent merges, `aggregate_version` as a dedup primitive, Delta Lake MERGE semantics, and how ordering + version together enforce the business invariant \"one final result per `(tenant, execution, test_case, attempt)` key.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "**Talking points:**\n",
    "- `aggregate_version` is monotonic per aggregate (here `tenant+execution+test_case+attempt`); MERGE keeps only the highest version seen.\n",
    "- MERGE is idempotent — re-running the same batch produces the same silver state.\n",
    "- Bronze append-only preserves the original envelope (event_time vs ingested_at); silver is the deduplicated, conformed view.\n",
    "- A real system would partition by `tenant_bucket` and `event_day` to avoid hot keys and small-file storms.\n",
    "- Streaming equivalent: Structured Streaming `foreachBatch` MERGE with checkpointed offsets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Prototype A — CDC dedup to silver (idempotent merge with aggregate_version)\n",
    "from pyspark.sql import functions as F\n",
    "from pyspark.sql.window import Window\n",
    "from delta.tables import DeltaTable\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    dbutils  # noqa: F401\n",
    "    ON_DATABRICKS = True\nexcept NameError:\n",
    "    ON_DATABRICKS = False\n",
    "\n",
    "CATALOG = \"main\"\n",
    "BRONZE = f\"{CATALOG}.demo_bronze\"\n",
    "SILVER = f\"{CATALOG}.demo_silver_results\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"ON_DATABRICKS={ON_DATABRICKS}\")\n",
    "print(f\"bronze={BRONZE}  silver={SILVER}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- 1. Synthetic bronze: out-of-order + duplicate CDC events ---\n",
    "bronze_rows = [\n",
    "    # tenant, exec, test_case, attempt, aggregate_version, event_time, ingested_at, status\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_login\", 1, 1, \"2026-10-01T10:00:00Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:00:05Z\", \"PENDING\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_login\", 1, 2, \"2026-10-01T10:00:30Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:00:31Z\", \"RUNNING\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_login\", 1, 3, \"2026-10-01T10:01:00Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:01:02Z\", \"PASSED\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_login\", 1, 3, \"2026-10-01T10:01:00Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:01:09Z\", \"PASSED\"),  # duplicate (same version)\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_login\", 1, 4, \"2026-10-01T10:01:15Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:01:20Z\", \"PASSED\"),  # higher version arrived later\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_search\", 1, 1, \"2026-10-01T10:00:10Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:00:12Z\", \"RUNNING\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_search\", 1, 2, \"2026-10-01T10:00:50Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:00:51Z\", \"FAILED\"),\n",
    "    (\"t2\", \"e1\", \"tc_home\", 1, 1, \"2026-10-01T10:00:00Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:00:01Z\", \"PASSED\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "schema = \"tenant_id STRING, execution_id STRING, test_case_id STRING, attempt_id INT, \" \\\n",
    "         \"aggregate_version INT, event_time TIMESTAMP, ingested_at TIMESTAMP, status STRING\"\n",
    "bronze_df = spark.createDataFrame(bronze_rows, schema=schema)\n",
    "\n",
    "if ON_DATABRICKS:\n",
    "    spark.sql(f\"CREATE CATALOG IF NOT EXISTS {CATALOG}\")\n",
    "    bronze_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(BRONZE)\n",
    "    display(bronze_df.orderBy(\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"aggregate_version\"))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"[local] bronze_df preview:\")\n",
    "    bronze_df.orderBy(\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"aggregate_version\").show(20, truncate=False)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- 2. Build silver: one row per business key, highest aggregate_version wins ---\n",
    "w = Window.partitionBy(\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\").orderBy(F.desc(\"aggregate_version\"), F.desc(\"ingested_at\"))\n",
    "silver_df = (\n",
    "    spark.read.format(\"delta\").table(BRONZE)\n",
    "    .withColumn(\"_rn\", F.row_number().over(w))\n",
    "    .filter(F.col(\"_rn\") == 1)\n",
    "    .drop(\"_rn\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "if ON_DATABRICKS:\n",
    "    silver_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"overwrite\").saveAsTable(SILVER)\n",
    "    display(spark.read.table(SILVER).orderBy(\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\"))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    silver_df_local = silver_df\n",
    "    print(\"[local] silver preview:\")\n",
    "    silver_df_local.show(20, truncate=False)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- 3. Idempotent MERGE on a second batch (proves re-runnability) ---\n",
    "delta_path = f\"/tmp/delta/{SILVER.replace('.', '_')}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# For local-mode demo we write silver to a parquet path and use DeltaTable over it if delta is available\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from delta.tables import DeltaTable\n",
    "    HAS_DELTA = True\nexcept Exception:\n",
    "    HAS_DELTA = False\n",
    "\n",
    "if ON_DATABRICKS and HAS_DELTA:\n",
    "    silver_tbl = DeltaTable.forName(spark, SILVER)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Local fallback: keep a pandas version of silver for assertions\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "new_batch_rows = [\n",
    "    # Same keys as before but with a *newer* aggregate_version and a corrected status\n",
    "    (\"t1\", \"e1\", \"tc_login\", 1, 5, \"2026-10-01T10:01:40Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:01:42Z\", \"PASSED\"),\n",
    "    # A new test case for t2\n",
    "    (\"t2\", \"e1\", \"tc_search\", 1, 1, \"2026-10-01T10:00:30Z\", \"2026-10-01T10:00:31Z\", \"PASSED\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "new_batch_df = spark.createDataFrame(new_batch_rows, schema=schema)\n",
    "if ON_DATABRICKS:\n",
    "    new_batch_df.write.format(\"delta\").mode(\"append\").saveAsTable(BRONZE)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"[local] would append new batch to bronze:\")\n",
    "    new_batch_df.show(truncate=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Rebuild silver with full re-merge semantics locally\n",
    "    from pyspark.sql import Row\n",
    "    all_bronze = spark.read.format(\"delta\").table(BRONZE) if ON_DATABRICKS else None\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "all_pd = pd.concat([\n",
    "    pd.DataFrame(bronze_rows, columns=schema.split(\", \")).assign(_src=\"batch1\"),\n",
    "    pd.DataFrame(new_batch_rows, columns=schema.split(\", \")).assign(_src=\"batch2\"),\n",
    "])\n",
    "all_pd[\"event_time\"] = pd.to_datetime(all_pd[\"event_time\"], utc=True)\n",
    "all_pd[\"ingested_at\"] = pd.to_datetime(all_pd[\"ingested_at\"], utc=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "silver_pd = (\n",
    "    all_pd.sort_values([\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"aggregate_version\", \"ingested_at\"],\n",
    "                       ascending=[True, True, True, True, False, False])\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates(subset=[\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\"], keep=\"first\")\n",
    "    .drop(columns=\"_src\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"silver after re-merge:\")\n",
    "print(silver_pd.sort_values([\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\"]).to_string(index=False))"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- 4. Assertions ---\n",
    "# One final row per (tenant, execution, test_case, attempt)\n",
    "key_cols = [\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\"]\n",
    "assert len(silver_pd) == silver_pd.drop_duplicates(key_cols).shape[0], \"duplicate business keys in silver\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Highest aggregate_version kept per key\n",
    "silver_pd_sorted = silver_pd.sort_values(\"aggregate_version\").drop_duplicates(key_cols, keep=\"last\")\n",
    "joined = silver_pd.merge(silver_pd_sorted[key_cols + [\"aggregate_version\"]].rename(columns={\"aggregate_version\": \"max_version\"}),\n",
    "                        on=key_cols, how=\"left\")\n",
    "assert (joined[\"aggregate_version\"] == joined[\"max_version\"]).all(), \"silver kept a stale aggregate_version\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Idempotency: re-applying the same batch must not change counts\n",
    "double = pd.concat([all_pd, all_pd])\n",
    "silver_double = (\n",
    "    double.sort_values([\"tenant_id\", \"execution_id\", \"test_case_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"aggregate_version\", \"ingested_at\"],\n",
    "                        ascending=[True, True, True, True, False, False])\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates(subset=key_cols, keep=\"first\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "assert len(silver_double) == len(silver_pd), \"re-applying same batch changed silver\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"[PASS] silver rows={len(silver_pd)} keys={len(silver_pd.drop_duplicates(key_cols))}\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Prototype B — Flakiness SQL runner (synthetic data)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this proves:** Given a synthetic `test_results` fact table with retries and environment variation, a single Spark SQL pipeline can compute **first-attempt failure rate**, **transition rate**, and **retry recovery rate** per `(tenant, project, test_case, environment)` — the canonical inputs to a flakiness score.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the panel tests:** Your ability to write correct window-function SQL, choose the right grain, ignore retries when computing transitions, and reason about how to extend this into a calibrated probabilistic flakiness score.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Talking points:**\n",
    "- Transitions are computed on **first attempts only** — retries must not artificially create flakiness.\n",
    "- `LAG(status)` partitioned by `(tenant, project, test_case, environment)` ordered by completion time yields transition pairs.\n",
    "- `retry_recovery_rate = recovered_on_retry / failed_first_attempts` quantifies whether the platform is hiding real failures behind retries.\n",
    "- Apply shrinkage / Bayesian prior for small samples; never declare a test \"flaky\" on two runs.\n",
    "- At scale: pre-aggregate to project-day, then join; avoid `LAG` over billions of rows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Prototype B — Flakiness SQL runner with synthetic data\n",
    "from pyspark.sql import functions as F\n",
    "from pyspark.sql.window import Window\n",
    "\n",
    "results_rows = [\n",
    # ten     project test        env      exec  att status    completed\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e1\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:00\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e2\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:10\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e3\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:20\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e4\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:30\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e5\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:40\"),\n",
    "    # tc_login in env-a: alternating → high transition rate\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_search\",\"env-a\",\"e1\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:00\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_search\",\"env-a\",\"e1\",2,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:05\"),  # retry recovered\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_search\",\"env-a\",\"e2\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:10\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_search\",\"env-a\",\"e3\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:20\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_search\",\"env-a\",\"e4\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:30\"),\n",
    "    # tc_search in env-a: reliably failing on first attempt, some retries recover\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_checkout\",\"env-a\",\"e1\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:00\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_checkout\",\"env-a\",\"e2\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:10\"),\n",
    "    (\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_checkout\",\"env-a\",\"e3\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:20\"),\n",
    "    # tc_checkout: stable pass\n",
    "    (\"t2\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e1\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:00\"),\n",
    "    (\"t2\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e2\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:10\"),\n",
    "    (\"t2\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e3\",1,\"FAILED\",\"2026-10-01 09:20\"),\n",
    "    (\"t2\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\",\"e4\",1,\"PASSED\",\"2026-10-01 09:30\"),\n",
    "    # t2/p1/tc_login: one transition in 4 runs\n",
    "]\n",
    "schema_b = \"tenant_id STRING, project_id STRING, test_case_id STRING, environment_hash STRING, \" \\\n",
    "           \"execution_id STRING, attempt_id INT, status STRING, completed_at TIMESTAMP\"\n",
    "df = spark.createDataFrame(results_rows, schema=schema_b)\n",
    "df.createOrReplaceTempView(\"test_results\")\n",
    "print(\"Synthetic test_results:\")\n",
    "df.show(20, truncate=False)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- 1. first_attempt_only with LAG() for transitions ---\n",
    "first_attempts = spark.sql(\"\"\"\n",
    "  SELECT tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash,\n",
    "         execution_id, attempt_id, status, completed_at,\n",
    "         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (\n",
    "           PARTITION BY tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash, execution_id\n",
    "           ORDER BY attempt_id\n",
    "         ) AS attempt_rank,\n",
    "         LAG(status) OVER (\n",
    "           PARTITION BY tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash\n",
    "           ORDER BY completed_at, execution_id\n",
    "         ) AS previous_status\n",
    "  FROM test_results\n",
    "  WHERE status IN ('PASSED','FAILED')\n",
    "\"\"\").filter(\"attempt_rank = 1\")\n",
    "first_attempts.createOrReplaceTempView(\"first_attempts\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- 2. execution_outcomes: did the first attempt fail? did any retry recover? ---\n",
    "exec_outcomes = spark.sql(\"\"\"\n",
    "  SELECT tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash,\n",
    "         execution_id,\n",
    "         MAX(CASE WHEN attempt_id = 1 AND status = 'FAILED' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS first_failed,\n",
    "         MAX(CASE WHEN status = 'PASSED' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS any_passed,\n",
    "         COUNT(*) AS attempt_count\n",
    "  FROM test_results\n",
    "  GROUP BY tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash, execution_id\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "exec_outcomes.createOrReplaceTempView(\"execution_outcomes\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- 3. stability + recovery aggregation per (tenant,project,test_case,environment) ---\n",
    "stability = spark.sql(\"\"\"\n",
    "  SELECT tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash,\n",
    "         COUNT(*) AS run_count,\n",
    "         AVG(CASE WHEN status='FAILED' THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS first_attempt_failure_rate,\n",
    "         AVG(CASE WHEN previous_status IS NULL THEN NULL\n",
    "                  WHEN status <> previous_status THEN 1.0 ELSE 0.0 END) AS transition_rate\n",
    "  FROM first_attempts\n",
    "  GROUP BY tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "stability.createOrReplaceTempView(\"stability\")\n",
    "\n",
    "recovery = spark.sql(\"\"\"\n",
    "  SELECT tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash,\n",
    "         SUM(first_failed) AS failed_first_attempts,\n",
    "         SUM(CASE WHEN first_failed=1 AND any_passed=1 AND attempt_count>1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS recovered_on_retry\n",
    "  FROM execution_outcomes\n",
    "  GROUP BY tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "recovery.createOrReplaceTempView(\"recovery\")\n",
    "\n",
    "result = spark.sql(\"\"\"\n",
    "  SELECT s.*, r.failed_first_attempts, r.recovered_on_retry,\n",
    "         CASE WHEN r.failed_first_attempts = 0 THEN NULL\n",
    "              ELSE r.recovered_on_retry * 1.0 / r.failed_first_attempts END AS retry_recovery_rate\n",
    "  FROM stability s\n",
    "  JOIN recovery r USING (tenant_id, project_id, test_case_id, environment_hash)\n",
    "  ORDER BY transition_rate DESC NULLS LAST, run_count DESC\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "result.createOrReplaceTempView(\"flakiness_signals\")\n",
    "result.show(20, truncate=False)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# --- 4. Assertions ---\n",
    "rows = [r.asDict() for r in result.collect()]\n",
    "by_key = {(r[\"tenant_id\"], r[\"project_id\"], r[\"test_case_id\"], r[\"environment_hash\"]): r for r in rows}\n",
    "\n",
    "# tc_login/env-a for t1/p1: transitions = PASSED->FAILED, FAILED->PASSED, PASSED->FAILED, FAILED->PASSED\n",
    "# 5 runs, 4 transitions (last run has no \"next\") → 1.0\n",
    "login_t1 = by_key[(\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\")]\n",
    "assert login_t1[\"run_count\"] == 5, login_t1\n",
    "assert abs(login_t1[\"transition_rate\"] - 1.0) < 1e-6, login_t1\n",
    "\n",
    "# tc_checkout/env-a for t1/p1: 3 runs all PASSED, no transitions, run_count>=10 → excluded by WHERE\n",
    "# ... we have no WHERE in the SQL above (intentionally, to demo signal on small data)\n",
    "checkout_t1 = by_key[(\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_checkout\",\"env-a\")]\n",
    "assert checkout_t1[\"run_count\"] == 3\n",
    "assert checkout_t1[\"transition_rate\"] is None or checkout_t1[\"transition_rate\"] == 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# t2/p1/tc_login: 4 runs, transitions = PASSED->PASSED (0), PASSED->FAILED (1), FAILED->PASSED (1) → 2/3 ≈ 0.667\n",
    "login_t2 = by_key[(\"t2\",\"p1\",\"tc_login\",\"env-a\")]\n",
    "assert login_t2[\"run_count\"] == 4\n",
    "assert abs(login_t2[\"transition_rate\"] - 2/3) < 1e-6, login_t2\n",
    "\n",
    "# tc_search/env-a for t1/p1: failed_first_attempts=4, retries that recovered=1 → 0.25\n",
    "search_t1 = by_key[(\"t1\",\"p1\",\"tc_search\",\"env-a\")]\n",
    "assert abs(search_t1[\"retry_recovery_rate\"] - 0.25) < 1e-6, search_t1\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"[PASS] flakiness signals validated:\")\n",
    "for k, v in by_key.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}  run_count={v['run_count']}  trans={v['transition_rate']}  recovery={v['retry_recovery_rate']}\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Prototype C — Reconciliation job (producer vs accepted vs silver vs served)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this proves:** A single Spark job can compare the producer's declared execution manifest against the accepted-events stream, the deduplicated silver table, and the served dashboard view — and emit a per-execution `reconciliation_status` that a dashboard can render instead of confidently showing the wrong number.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the panel tests:** Your grasp of end-to-end data correctness, the difference between transport-level data and business-level state, and the operating model for surfacing \"data incomplete\" instead of silently publishing wrong numbers.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Talking points:**\n",
    "- Four layers: **producer manifest** (what the system said happened) → **accepted events** (what arrived) → **silver** (deduplicated truth) → **served** (what the dashboard rendered).\n",
    "- Mismatches have severity: missing in served is worse than a transient accepted lag.\n",
    "- `severity_1` is reserved for cross-tenant exposure or material executive-metric errors.\n",
    "- Reconciliation is a data product with its own SLO, owner, and runbook — not a side script.\n",
    "- Wire the status into the dashboard itself; silence is worse than an amber warning."
