    "## Prototype D — Retrieval evaluation harness (pure Python, no Spark)\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this proves:** A retrieval system can be evaluated offline with **recall@k**, **MRR**, **cross-tenant leakage = 0**, and **citation-correctness** before any model or LLM is involved — and the same harness survives a swap of the underlying retriever.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the panel tests:** Your understanding that RAG without an offline eval harness is gambling; that retrieval metrics can move in the wrong direction (higher recall, lower answer quality); that cross-tenant leakage is a non-negotiable invariant; and that you would gate any retrieval change on a stratified, versioned evaluation set.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Talking points:**\n",
    "- The eval set must stratify by tenant, failure category, framework, language, and adversarial inputs.\n",
    "- `recall@k`, `MRR`, `nDCG`, **exact-evidence-coverage**, **citation-correctness** are the four metrics that matter.\n",
    "- `cross_tenant_leakage` must be exactly 0 — this is a **release gate**, not a metric to \"improve.\"\n",
    "- Calibrate and prefer deterministic preprocessing over fancier retrieval.\n",
    "- Treat the eval set as a **versioned product**; breaking it invalidates prior comparisons."
   ]
  },
